1
00:00:00,970 --> 00:00:02,310
An inspector walks in…

2
00:00:02,350 --> 00:00:05,010
and asks to see your registers.

3
00:00:05,433 --> 00:00:08,488
With Eikon, they're already in order.

4
00:00:09,209 --> 00:00:10,444
Open Registers.

5
00:00:10,944 --> 00:00:13,084
Today's registers lists what is due,

6
00:00:13,124 --> 00:00:14,844
and what is done.

7
00:00:15,406 --> 00:00:16,516
For the fridge,

8
00:00:16,586 --> 00:00:18,906
type the lowest and the highest…

9
00:00:18,946 --> 00:00:21,256
one tap, and it's logged.

10
00:00:22,054 --> 00:00:25,064
Every daily register works the same way:

11
00:00:25,159 --> 00:00:27,124
a month, at a glance.

12
00:00:27,522 --> 00:00:28,422
A missed day…

13
00:00:28,462 --> 00:00:29,942
stands out.

14
00:00:30,278 --> 00:00:33,068
When the month is over, sign it off.

15
00:00:33,158 --> 00:00:36,148
Your name, and the date, on record.

16
00:00:37,317 --> 00:00:39,937
Controlled drugs are kept by medicine.

17
00:00:40,077 --> 00:00:42,117
In, out, and the running balance,

18
00:00:42,157 --> 00:00:43,837
line by line.

19
00:00:44,381 --> 00:00:47,066
If more went out than came in…

20
00:00:47,106 --> 00:00:48,446
it tells you.

21
00:00:48,526 --> 00:00:49,846
Count it now.

22
00:00:50,897 --> 00:00:52,802
Before an inspector comes,

23
00:00:52,842 --> 00:00:55,382
the Inspection check reads every register…

24
00:00:55,422 --> 00:00:58,522
and tells you exactly what to put right.

25
00:00:58,884 --> 00:01:00,114
Then, one tap…

26
00:01:00,154 --> 00:01:02,074
prints the whole pack.

27
00:01:02,164 --> 00:01:03,379
Every register.

28
00:01:03,419 --> 00:01:04,564
Every signature.

29
00:01:04,604 --> 00:01:05,734
In order.

30
00:01:06,623 --> 00:01:09,678
Eikon. Ready, before they walk in.

